```c
u8 __iomem ports[] = {
	idio16gpio->reg->out0_7, idio16gpio->reg->out8_15,
	idio16gpio->reg->in0_7, idio16gpio->reg->in8_15,
};
```
Reason:
The `ports` array was incorrectly defined to directly store the values of the device I/O registers instead of their addresses. This led to the `ioread8` function receiving incorrect memory offsets, resulting in improper memory access during the `get_multiple` callback.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```c
void __iomem *ports[] = {
	&idio16gpio->reg->out0_7, &idio16gpio->reg->out8_15,
	&idio16gpio->reg->in0_7, &idio16gpio->reg->in8_15,
};
port_state = ioread8(ports[i]);
```
Reason:
The `ports` array was changed to store the addresses of the device I/O registers by using the address-of operator (`&`). This ensures that the `ioread8` function receives the correct memory offsets, allowing it to read from the intended memory locations properly.

